  "statement": "Evaluate\n$$\\sum_{n=1}^{100}\\log_{10}\\left(3^{1-n}\\right).$$",
  "options": ["$-4950\\log_{10}3$", "$4950\\log_{10}3$", "$-5050\\log_{10}3$", "$5050\\log_{10}3$", "$1-4950\\log_{10}3$", "$1+4950\\log_{10}3$", "$1-5050\\log_{10}3$"],
  "answer": "A",
  "solution": "Using the power rule, $\\log_{10}(3^{1-n})=(1-n)\\log_{10}3$. So\n$$\\sum_{n=1}^{100}\\log_{10}(3^{1-n})=\\log_{10}3\\sum_{n=1}^{100}(1-n).$$\n\nNow $\\sum_{n=1}^{100}(1-n)=100-(1+2+\\cdots+100)=100-5050=-4950$, using $1+2+\\cdots+100=\\tfrac{100\\cdot101}{2}=5050$.\n\nTherefore the sum is $-4950\\log_{10}3$.\n\nThe answer is **A**.",
